\textbf{Solution:} Solve: The parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+\frac{5}{2}$ intersects the line $AB$ at point $A\left(-1, 0\right)$ and $B\left(4, \frac{5}{2}\right)$,\\
$\therefore \left\{\begin{array}{l}
0=a(-1)^{2}-b+\frac{5}{2}\\
\frac{5}{2}=16a+4b+\frac{5}{2}
\end{array}\right.$,\\
Solving, we get: $\left\{\begin{array}{l}
a=-\frac{1}{2}\\
b=2
\end{array}\right.$,\\
$\therefore$ the equation of the parabola is $\boxed{y=-\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+2x+\frac{5}{2}}$.
